Subject: [PATCH] avb: reject unresolved hashtree mode in release builds

The assertion is compiled out in this release configuration, leaving
uninitialized mode pointers when an unresolved/unknown mode is received.
Return INVALID_ARGUMENT for this invalid path; valid mode semantics are
unchanged. Do not disable Clang's uninitialized-value diagnostic.
Applies to EDK2 aef4e86045bd151a54d33bab8ae5e8e62462a8f4.

diff --git a/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/libavb/avb_cmdline.c b/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/libavb/avb_cmdline.c
index cca043f..5952631 100644
--- a/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/libavb/avb_cmdline.c
+++ b/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/libavb/avb_cmdline.c
@@ -408,11 +408,13 @@ AvbSlotVerifyResult avb_append_options(
         verity_mode = "logging";
         dm_verity_mode = "ignore_corruption";
         break;
+      default:
       case AVB_HASHTREE_ERROR_MODE_MANAGED_RESTART_AND_EIO:
         // Should never get here because MANAGED_RESTART_AND_EIO is
         // remapped by avb_manage_hashtree_error_mode().
         avb_assert_not_reached();
-        break;
+        ret = AVB_SLOT_VERIFY_RESULT_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT;
+        goto out;
       case AVB_HASHTREE_ERROR_MODE_PANIC:
         verity_mode = "panicking";
         dm_verity_mode = "panic_on_corruption";
